From: Parasite Eve <parasiteeve@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:48:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] GL renderer: attach decoded HD texture replacements

The GL renderer's frame boundary only called texture_tracker_endFrame, which
doesn't drain the texture IO responses. The Vulkan renderer drains and attaches
them in texture_tracker_on_queues_reset, from reset_queue, and the GL renderer
never called it: replacements were found on disk, requested and decoded, but
never bound, so the GL renderer always drew the original textures.

Call texture_tracker_on_queues_reset at the GL frame boundary, after the final
flush, while texture tracking is on.
---
 rhi/rhi_lib_gl.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rhi/rhi_lib_gl.c b/rhi/rhi_lib_gl.c
index 103ba6a..09a52d2 100644
--- a/rhi/rhi_lib_gl.c
+++ b/rhi/rhi_lib_gl.c
@@ -6409,6 +6409,13 @@ void rhi_gl_finalize_frame(const void *fb, unsigned width,
     * out this frame has been consumed. */
    if (renderer->tracker)
    {
+      /* What the Vulkan renderer does from reset_queue: drain the decoded IO
+       * responses and attach them to their uploads. Without it no replacement
+       * ever binds in the GL renderer: every load is requested and decoded, but
+       * never picked up. Every handle of this frame has been consumed by the
+       * flush above, as texture_tracker_on_queues_reset requires. */
+      if (renderer->texture_tracking_enabled)
+         texture_tracker_on_queues_reset(renderer->tracker);
       texture_tracker_endFrame(renderer->tracker);
       renderer->hd_handle = hd_handle_make_none();
    }
